The learner reads the first subscript as a row and the second as a column, checks whether both exist, and reads their intersection or selects “No such entry.” Tutorial 34f3a63d-a273-50fb-b26a-ae172c7e93e9 explicitly says “The first subscript represents the row and the second subscript represents the column.” Tutorial 775ac64e-8b63-5c51-824d-1d99d17a2a0a defines entries for i=1,…,m and j=1,…,n. The prerequisite is counting matrix rows and columns; no matrix arithmetic is assessed.

Source 622baf41-fe35-55ee-bfc6-f1e6a2cb089a asks for a23=-3 in a 2×4 matrix. Source 8904abf3-dbf2-549a-8f8b-9fbdb7308ad3 asks for e31=-3 in a 3×2 matrix with the complete five-number bank {1,-3,4,-1,5}. Source 01081318-5aef-53ec-b42a-cf09d90e23dc offers a numeric target and “No such entry”; 5bfd6a33-c881-55bc-8200-148d7f57a946 asks for a row outside the matrix. Those two originals lack keys and worked solutions; raw replay preserves the omissions. The latter supports an authored bounds-check explanation. The other five practice records have easy labels; the two missing labels remain missing in raw replay. The current source capture agrees with the bundled replay mathematics. Raw replay preserves every complete bank, including opaque external 0 and 2 alternatives, without claiming to know their intended misconception.

The response remains one radio choice from five, or a scalar blank for an existing entry. The requested band is easy. Existing moderate/hard authored visual-scan APIs remain untouched by this targeted repair; they are not evidence for new source difficulty labels. Nonsquare shapes distinguish this knowledge point from its square-matrix neighbor. Positive one-digit indices and signed one-digit entries preserve the source notation and reading workload. Easy dimensions are the observed 2×3, 2×4, 3×2, 3×4 and 5×4. No source question or output for this skill uses a diagram; the route-map prerequisite is context, not part of this task.

Answer-bearing assignments are the target row/column, whether it exists, its value, and the keyed option. Every cell is eligible. A single index one beyond its dimension is the existing conservative overflow extension; both row and column overflow must be exercised. Blank fields and numeric-only banks require an existing entry because neither can express absence. Otherwise layout, label and option position must not determine existence. Numeric values, labels and irrelevant entries may vary without changing the method. Target changes must update the prompt, solution and key together.

The numeric-only profile keeps its four-cell rectangle plus a fifth distinct location. With three or more columns it uses another nearby column; with two columns it uses another nearby row. For the source 3×2 target this yields the complete original bank. This transposed neighbor rule changes no learner operation and avoids excluding all two-column matrices. Duplicate locations or values still reject the whole bank.

Radio layout will be selected independently of numeric versus absent targets. The legacy inline_no_entry_radio name remains an API alias for an inline layout, not a restriction on the correct response. Explicit compatible profiles remain available in every radio layout. Normal single-record sampling selects the bank/decision case before sampling compatible values.

Finite batches need witnesses to both existence cases within each represented radio layout that offers “No such entry.” The easy CLI will construct shuffled contrasting pairs in a shared randomly selected layout, choosing valid and overflow profiles before values. Additional slots choose another contrasting pair or the source blank or numeric-only family. Any final unpaired slot uses a blank or numeric-only bank, so it cannot introduce an unpaired layout-based absence cue. This coverage rule is motivated by the demonstrated elimination shortcut, not a target answer-frequency quota. A one-record request cannot exhibit both cases and retains ordinary sampling. Explicit profile requests retain their stated case restriction. Pair order and option order are shuffled. All layouts, target positions, shapes, and supported banks remain reachable, and each item stands alone.

